invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_init leaves the key's cpu byte as its storage held it,
  so a key that no call gave a description of the CPU, a header
  protection key among them, reads whatever the stack held, and gcm.c
  would pick the VAES kernels from it. bin/aes_runtime_test fills the key
  with 0xff before the call and requires the byte to read 0 after it.

--- old
    // No kernel until aes_traffic_key_cpu names the session's CPU.
    k->key.cpu = 0;
--- new
